<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Credit Memorandum — South River Capital — {{ name }}</title>
<style>
:root{--navy:#0f2a43;--navy-2:#1c3d5a;--gold:#b9952b;--ink:#1a1a1a;--ink-soft:#444;--rule:#cdd3da;--rule-strong:#9aa6b2;--paper:#fff;--desk:#e9e7e0;--zebra:#f4f6f8;}
*{box-sizing:border-box;}html,body{margin:0;padding:0;}
body{background:var(--desk);font-family:"Times New Roman",Times,serif;font-size:10pt;line-height:1.42;color:var(--ink);-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;padding:32px 16px 64px;}
.page{width:8.5in;min-height:11in;background:var(--paper);margin:0 auto 28px;padding:.7in .75in .85in;box-shadow:0 2px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.12);border-radius:2px;position:relative;}
p{margin:0 0 7pt;text-wrap:pretty;}.lead{margin-bottom:9pt;}strong{font-weight:bold;}
.section{margin-top:16pt;}.section:first-of-type{margin-top:0;}
h2.sec{font-size:11.5pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:0 0 8pt;padding-bottom:4pt;border-bottom:1.5pt solid var(--navy);display:flex;align-items:baseline;gap:8pt;}
h2.sec .num{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:bold;color:#fff;background:var(--navy);padding:2pt 5pt;letter-spacing:.05em;transform:translateY(-1pt);}
h3.sub{font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;margin:11pt 0 4pt;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.03em;}
.masthead{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-start;border-bottom:3px solid var(--navy);padding-bottom:10pt;margin-bottom:4pt;}
.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:11px;}.brand .brand-logo{height:50px;width:auto;display:block;background:#fff;padding:5px 8px;border-radius:4px;}
.brand .wm{line-height:1;}.brand .wm .name{font-size:16pt;font-weight:bold;color:var(--navy);letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;}
.brand .wm .tag{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;letter-spacing:.32em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:4px;font-weight:bold;}
.doc-meta{text-align:right;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;}
.doc-meta .conf{font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.18em;color:#fff;background:var(--gold);padding:2pt 6pt;display:inline-block;text-transform:uppercase;}
.doc-meta .dt{font-size:8pt;color:var(--ink-soft);margin-top:6pt;}.doc-meta .dt span{color:var(--ink);font-weight:bold;}
.doc-title{text-align:center;margin:14pt 0 16pt;}.doc-title .kicker{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7.5pt;letter-spacing:.4em;color:var(--gold);text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:bold;}
.doc-title h1{font-size:21pt;font-weight:bold;color:#000;letter-spacing:.04em;margin:5pt 0 0;text-transform:uppercase;}
table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:4pt 0 6pt;font-size:9.5pt;}
caption{caption-side:top;text-align:left;font-weight:bold;color:#000;padding-bottom:3pt;font-size:9.5pt;}
th,td{border:.75pt solid var(--rule);padding:3.5pt 7pt;vertical-align:top;text-align:left;}
thead th{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7.5pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;border-color:var(--navy-2);}
table.kv td.k{width:30%;background:#f1f4f7;font-weight:bold;color:#000;white-space:nowrap;}
table.kv.two td.k{width:22%;}
.num-col{text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap;}
tbody tr.total td{font-weight:bold;background:#eef1f4;border-top:1.25pt solid var(--rule-strong);}
tbody tr.grand td{font-weight:bold;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;border-color:var(--navy-2);}
.zebra tbody tr:nth-child(even) td{background:var(--zebra);}
/* In zebra tables the even-row stripe outranks tr.grand's navy background (equal
   specificity, later rule), leaving white text on a light stripe whenever the
   grand row lands on an even index. Re-assert the navy band at higher specificity
   so the Section VIII Net Cash Flow row always matches the other grand rows
   (Lauren, 2026-07-28). Literal colors, not var(), so the row also survives
   Word's HTML engine (which drops var() backgrounds — see render_word). */
.zebra tbody tr.grand td{background:#0f2a43;color:#fff;border-color:#1c3d5a;}
.src-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:9pt;margin-top:8pt;}
.src{border:.75pt solid var(--rule);border-top:2.5pt solid var(--navy);padding:7pt 9pt;background:#fafbfc;}
.src .lab{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7pt;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:bold;color:#000;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:4pt;}
.src .ord{font-size:8pt;color:#000;font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;margin-bottom:2pt;}
.callout{border-left:3pt solid #000;background:#fcfbf6;padding:9pt 12pt;margin:6pt 0 8pt;}
ul.tight{margin:3pt 0 7pt;padding-left:18pt;}ul.tight li{margin-bottom:3pt;}
.faq{margin-bottom:9pt;}.faq .q{font-weight:bold;color:#000;margin-bottom:2pt;}
.note-fine{font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--ink-soft);}
.pg-footer{position:absolute;left:.75in;right:.75in;bottom:.42in;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.8pt;letter-spacing:.1em;color:#8a8a8a;text-transform:uppercase;border-top:.75pt solid var(--rule);padding-top:5pt;}
/* Deal Summary & Policy Compliance coversheet (page 1). Literal colors on the
   status boxes (not var()) so they survive Word's HTML engine — see render_word. */
.cover-title{margin:8pt 0 8pt;}
.cover-title h1{font-size:17pt;}
.cover-sec{margin-top:9pt;}
.cover-sec h2.sec{margin-bottom:5pt;}
.cover-sec h3.sub{margin-top:0;}
/* Rule 15 — each financed debt listed under the summary liability it rolls into: indented, lighter, and hairline-ruled so it reads as a breakdown of the line above rather than another liability. */tbody tr.dsc td{background:#fbfcfd;font-size:8.5pt;color:var(--ink-soft);border-top-width:.4pt;border-top-style:dotted;padding-top:2.5pt;padding-bottom:2.5pt;}tbody tr.dsc td.dsc-lbl{padding-left:26pt;}.dsc-note{display:block;font-size:7.5pt;color:#6b7683;}table.compliance{font-size:8pt;line-height:1.25;margin:2pt 0 4pt;}
table.compliance td{padding:2pt 5pt;}
table.compliance thead th{font-size:7pt;padding:2.5pt 5pt;}
.st-cell{white-space:nowrap;}
.st{display:inline-block;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:6.5pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.05em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#9aa6b2;border:.75pt solid #cdd3da;background:#fff;padding:1pt 4pt;margin-right:3pt;}
.st:last-child{margin-right:0;}
.st.on{background:#0f2a43;border-color:#1c3d5a;color:#fff;}
.cover-sec .callout{padding:6pt 10pt;margin:3pt 0 4pt;font-size:8.5pt;}
.approval{display:flex;gap:24pt;margin-top:10pt;break-inside:avoid;}
.approval .sig{flex:1;}
.approval .sig-date{flex:0 0 1.5in;}
.approval .line{border-bottom:1pt solid #1a1a1a;height:14pt;}
.approval .cap{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:7pt;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#444;margin-top:3pt;}
@page{size:letter;margin:.7in .75in .6in;}
@media print{body{background:none;padding:0;}.page{width:auto;min-height:0;margin:0;padding:0;box-shadow:none;border-radius:0;break-after:page;}.page:last-child{break-after:auto;}.pg-footer{display:none;}.section,.faq,.src,.callout,tr,thead{break-inside:avoid;}h2.sec,h3.sub{break-after:avoid;}th,td,thead th,tbody tr.grand td,.brand .brand-logo,.doc-meta .conf,h2.sec .num,.src,.st{-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact;print-color-adjust:exact;}}
</style></head>
<body style="background-color:rgba(255,255,253,0.98)">
<div class="page">
<header class="masthead"><div class="brand"><img class="brand-logo" src="{{ logo }}" alt="South River Capital"></div><div class="doc-meta"><div class="dt">Memo Date: <span>{{ md_fmt }}</span></div></div></header>
<div class="doc-title cover-title"><div class="kicker">South River Capital</div><h1>Deal Summary &amp; Policy Compliance</h1></div>
<table class="kv two"><tbody>
<tr><td class="k">Borrower</td><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="k">{% if contracted_income_money %}Contracted Income{% else %}Qualifying Income{% endif %}</td><td>{{ income_basis_money }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Business / Employer</td><td>{{ employer }}{% if industry %} &mdash; {{ industry }}{% endif %}</td><td class="k">LTI</td><td>{{ lti }}%</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Loan</td><td>{{ loan_money }} at {{ rate }}% per annum</td><td class="k">Term</td><td>{{ months }}-month balloon &mdash; matures {{ mat_fmt }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Collateral</td><td>{{ collateral_cell }}{% if collateral_money %} ({{ collateral_money }}){% endif %} &middot; personal guarantee &middot; {% if has_ins %}life/disability policy{% else %}No Insurance{% endif %}</td><td class="k">{% if ltv %}LTV{% else %}Repayment{% endif %}</td><td>{% if ltv %}{{ ltv }}%{% else %}Balloon at maturity{% endif %}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Borrower Profile</td><td>{{ profile_label }}</td><td class="k">{% if dscr %}DSCR{% else %}Repayment{% endif %}</td><td>{% if dscr %}{{ dscr }}x{% else %}Balloon at maturity{% endif %}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<section class="section cover-sec"><h2 class="sec">Policy Compliance</h2>
<table class="zebra compliance"><thead><tr><th>Criteria / Covenant</th><th style="width:78px">Requirement</th><th>Actual</th><th style="width:104px">Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ compliance_html }}</tbody></table></section>
<section class="section cover-sec"><h3 class="sub">Exceptions &amp; Mitigants</h3>
<div class="callout">{{ exceptions_html }}</div></section>
<div class="approval"><div class="sig"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Credit Approval &mdash; Exceptions Acknowledged</div></div><div class="sig sig-date"><div class="line"></div><div class="cap">Date</div></div></div>
<p class="note-fine" style="margin-top:6pt;font-size:7.5pt">Thresholds per South River Capital non-sports lending guidelines; any exception requires credit approval prior to funding. {{ provisional }}</p>
<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page 1 of 7</span></div>
</div>
<div class="page">
<header class="masthead"><div class="brand"><img class="brand-logo" src="{{ logo }}" alt="South River Capital"></div><div class="doc-meta"><div class="dt">Memo Date: <span>{{ md_fmt }}</span></div></div></header>
<div class="doc-title"><div class="kicker">South River Capital</div><h1>Credit Memorandum</h1></div>
<table class="kv two"><tbody>
<tr><td class="k">Borrower</td><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="k">Industry</td><td>{{ industry }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Address</td><td>{{ addr }}</td><td class="k">Loan Type</td><td>{{ loan_type }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Phone</td><td>{{ phone }}</td><td class="k">Date of Birth</td><td>{{ dob }}</td></tr>
<tr><td class="k">Business / Employer</td><td>{{ employer }}</td><td class="k">Tax&nbsp;ID / Driver's&nbsp;Lic.</td><td>{{ ssn }} / {{ dl }}</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">I</span>Purpose of Proposed Facility</h2>
<div class="callout"><p>The Borrower is requesting a <strong>{{ loan_money }}</strong> loan{% if contracted_income_money %} as an advance against <strong>{{ contracted_income_money }}</strong> in contracted income{% else %} supported by <strong>{{ income_money }}</strong> in annual qualifying income{% endif %}.
{% if profile == 'business' %}{{ name }} is {{ occupation }} at {{ employer }}{% if industry %}, a {{ industry }} business{% endif %}. Repayment is supported by the income the Borrower draws from the business, as documented in the tax returns and financial statements on file.
{% elif profile == 'investment' %}{{ name }} holds income-producing assets through {{ employer }}{% if industry %} ({{ industry }}){% endif %}. Repayment is supported by net income from those assets{% if collateral_money %}, and the facility is secured by {{ collateral_desc or 'the pledged collateral' }} valued at <strong>{{ collateral_money }}</strong>{% endif %}.
{% else %}{{ name }} is {{ occupation }} at {{ employer }}. Repayment is supported by documented personal income.{% endif %}
The facility is structured to balloon in <strong>{{ mat_fmt }}</strong>.</p></div>
<div class="src-grid"><div class="src"><div class="lab">Primary</div><div class="ord">Repayment Source</div><p style="margin:0">{% if profile == 'business' %}Cash flow from the Borrower's business income.{% elif profile == 'investment' %}Net income from the Borrower's income-producing assets.{% else %}The Borrower's documented personal income.{% endif %}</p></div><div class="src"><div class="lab">Secondary</div><div class="ord">Repayment Source</div><p style="margin:0">{% if collateral_money %}Liquidation of the pledged collateral, and enforcement of the full personal guarantee provided by the Borrower.{% else %}Enforcement of the full personal guarantee provided by the Borrower.{% endif %}</p></div>{% if has_ins %}<div class="src"><div class="lab">Tertiary</div><div class="ord">Repayment Source</div><p style="margin:0">Life / disability insurance policy assigned to Lender.</p></div>{% endif %}</div></section>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">II</span>Recommendation &amp; Action Request</h2>
<h3 class="sub">Summary of Transaction Recommendations</h3>
<ul class="tight"><li>Lender to provide a <strong>{{ loan_money }}</strong> loan at <strong>{{ rate }}%</strong> per annum based on the Borrower's documented income{% if collateral_money %} and the pledged collateral{% endif %}.</li><li>Borrower to authorize ACH debit from an operating account for automatic payment of each scheduled installment.</li><li>Lender to file a UCC-1 financing statement against {% if collateral_money %}the pledged collateral{% else %}the Borrower's business assets{% endif %}.</li>{% if collateral_money %}<li>Lender to obtain a third-party appraisal or valuation of the pledged collateral prior to funding.</li>{% endif %}{% if has_ins %}<li>Lender to be protected by a life / disability insurance policy assigned to Lender.</li>{% endif %}</ul>
<h3 class="sub">Action Request Details</h3>
<ul class="tight"><li>Lender to provide a <strong>{{ months }}</strong>-month full balloon loan; all principal and interest due at maturity {{ mat_fmt }}.</li><li>Borrower to authorize ACH debit from an operating account for automatic payment.</li><li>Lender to file a UCC-1 financing statement against {% if collateral_money %}the pledged collateral{% else %}the Borrower's business assets{% endif %}.</li>{% if advisor %}<li>Borrower's adviser: <strong>{{ advisor }}</strong></li>{% endif %}</ul></section>
<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page 2 of 7</span></div>
</div>
<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">III</span>New Facility Terms &amp; Conditions</h2>
<table class="kv"><tbody><tr><td class="k">Borrower</td><td>{{ name }}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Relationship</td><td>{{ loan_type }} Borrower</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Loan Type</td><td>{% if profile == 'business' %}Business-income loan{% elif profile == 'investment' %}Asset-secured loan{% else %}Personal income loan{% endif %}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Purpose</td><td>Business purposes</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Proposed Commitment</td><td>{{ loan_money }}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Proposed Maturity</td><td>{{ mat_fmt }}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Amortization Schedule</td><td>Balloon</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Balloon at Maturity</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Upfront Fee</td><td>{{ fee }}% ({{ fee_amt }})</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Interest Rate</td><td>{{ rate }}%</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Prepayment Penalty</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Collateral</td><td>{% if collateral_money %}{{ collateral_desc or 'Pledged collateral' }} &mdash; UCC-1 filing{% else %}Unsecured &mdash; personal guarantee; UCC-1 filing against business assets{% endif %}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Appraisals</td><td>{% if collateral_money %}Third-party valuation of pledged collateral &mdash; condition of closing{% else %}None{% endif %}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Formulas / Advances</td><td>LTI (Loan-to-Income): {{ loan_money }} loan &divide; {{ income_basis_money }} {% if contracted_income_money %}contracted income{% else %}annual qualifying income{% endif %} = <strong>{{ lti }}%</strong>{% if ltv %}<br>LTV (Loan-to-Value): {{ loan_money }} loan &divide; {{ collateral_money }} collateral = <strong>{{ ltv }}%</strong>{% endif %}{% if dscr %}<br>DSCR: cash available for debt service &divide; total debt service = <strong>{{ dscr }}x</strong>{% endif %}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Guarantor(s)</td><td>{{ name }}</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Subordinations</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td class="k">Repayment</td><td>{% if profile == 'business' %}Business income{% elif profile == 'investment' %}Net income from income-producing assets{% else %}Documented personal income{% endif %} &middot; enforcement of personal guarantee{% if collateral_money %} &middot; pledged collateral{% endif %}{% if has_ins %} &middot; life/disability policy assigned to Lender{% endif %}</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">IV</span>Risk Considerations &amp; FAQ</h2>
{% if profile == 'business' %}
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the business loses its largest customers?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Customer concentration is the principal risk to a closely held business's income. The concentration shown in the financial statements on file is confirmed at underwriting, and a material loss of revenue is a reportable event under the loan documents.</li><li>The facility is underwritten against documented historical income, not projected revenue, so a decline is measured against figures the Borrower has already achieved.</li></ul></div>
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if business income falls or the business operates at a loss?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Owner income varies with the business. The qualifying income is taken from the most recent complete tax year as filed, with prior years and the trend disclosed in the Income Analysis, so the underwriting basis is a documented figure rather than a favourable one.</li><li>The Borrower's personal guarantee reaches assets outside the business, and the Personal Financial Statement is the measure of that support.</li></ul></div>
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the Borrower dies, is disabled, or leaves the business?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Key-person risk is concentrated in a closely held business: the income underwritten here depends on the Borrower's continued involvement.</li>{% if has_ins %}<li>The Lender is assigned a separate life / disability insurance policy naming only the Lender.</li>{% else %}<li>No policy is assigned on this facility; the guarantee and the Borrower's estate are the support.</li>{% endif %}</ul></div>
{% elif profile == 'investment' %}
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the properties sit vacant or tenants stop paying?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Vacancy and tenant default are the principal risks to rental income. The qualifying income is net of operating expenses, taxes, insurance and existing mortgage debt service, so it is not a gross-rent figure.</li><li>Leases and the rent roll on file are confirmed at underwriting, and the lease terms relative to the facility's maturity are disclosed in the Income Analysis.</li></ul></div>
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the collateral falls in value?</div><ul class="tight"><li>{% if collateral_money %}The facility advances {{ ltv }}% against a {{ collateral_money }} third-party valuation, leaving equity ahead of the Lender's position.{% else %}No specific collateral is pledged on this facility; it rests on the personal guarantee.{% endif %}</li><li>A valuation obtained for this loan is a condition of closing, and the Lender holds a first-lien position by UCC-1 filing{% if collateral_money %} and, for real property, a recorded mortgage or deed of trust{% endif %}.</li></ul></div>
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the Borrower cannot refinance or sell at maturity?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Balloon maturity carries refinancing risk. The exit is sale or refinance of the asset, and the equity cushion above is what makes either available.</li><li>The Borrower's other liquid assets, as shown on the Personal Financial Statement, are the secondary path to repayment.</li></ul></div>
{% else %}
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the Borrower loses their job or their income is interrupted?</div><ul class="tight"><li>Income interruption is the principal risk on a facility carried by personal income. The qualifying income is documented from returns, W-2s and pay stubs rather than projected.</li><li>The Borrower's liquid assets, as shown on the Personal Financial Statement, are the first support through an interruption.</li></ul></div>
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the Borrower dies or is disabled?</div><ul class="tight"><li>{% if has_ins %}The Lender is assigned a separate life / disability insurance policy naming only the Lender.{% else %}No policy is assigned on this facility; the guarantee and the Borrower's estate are the support.{% endif %}</li></ul></div>
{% endif %}
<div class="faq"><div class="q">What if the Borrower over-leverages and becomes insolvent?</div><ul class="tight"><li>The Lender holds a first right of refusal on all additional debt; failure to comply is an event of default.</li><li>ACH debit on each due date repays Lender from the operating account before other discretionary uses.</li><li>Periodic credit report pulls &mdash; any new leverage triggers an event of default.</li></ul></div>
</section>
<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page 3 of 7</span></div>
</div>
<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">V</span>Borrower Background</h2><p class="lead">{{ background_text }}</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">VI</span>Uses of Funds</h2>
<p>The disbursement of the proposed facility is set out below.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Disbursement</th><th class="num-col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ uses_html }}</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine">Disbursement amounts are estimates sourced from the deal documents; confirm against the final settlement statement.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">VII</span>Income Analysis</h2>
{% if income_notes %}<p>{{ income_notes }}</p>{% endif %}
<p>{{ name }} has documented annual qualifying income of <strong>{{ income_money }}</strong>{% if employer %} from {{ employer }}{% endif %}.{% if contracted_income_money %} Of that, <strong>{{ contracted_income_money }}</strong> is committed by contract or lease over the term of this facility and serves as the LTI basis.{% endif %}</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Basis</th><th class="num-col">Amount</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% if contracted_income_money %}<tr><td>Contracted Income (facility term)</td><td class="num-col">{{ contracted_income_money }}</td><td>Committed by contract / lease</td></tr>{% endif %}<tr class="total"><td><strong>Underwriting Basis (Qualifying Income)</strong></td><td class="num-col"><strong>{{ income_money }}</strong></td><td>Documented &mdash; annual</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine">Figures reflect documented, recurring income only, per South River Capital underwriting policy. Projections, capital gains and non-recurring items are excluded.</p></section>
<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page 4 of 7</span></div>
</div>
<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">VIII</span>Guarantor Analysis</h2>
<p>The analysis below is based on the Borrower's documented income and the Personal Financial Statement on file. After servicing all existing debt, the Borrower maintains the net cash flow shown below.</p>
<table class="zebra"><caption>Personal Cash Flow Analysis &mdash; {{ name }}</caption><thead><tr><th style="width:34px">Note</th><th>Line Item</th><th class="num-col">Annual</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ cf_html }}</tbody></table>
<p class="note-fine"><strong>Notes:</strong>&nbsp; 1 &mdash; Annual qualifying income, documented and recurring. &nbsp;2 &mdash; Other income per Annual Income section of PFS. &nbsp;3 &mdash; Estimated 45% blended tax rate applied to gross income. &nbsp;4 &mdash; Estimated 10% of gross income to cover all ordinary living expenses. &nbsp;5 &mdash; Proposed Facility shown at principal (loan amount); the interest-included total is carried as a liability on the Personal Financial Statement. Alimony/child support and all other debt line items sourced from the Annual Expenditures section of the PFS and supporting documents.</p></section>
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">IX</span>Personal Financial Statement</h2>
<table><caption>As reported on Personal Financial Statement &mdash; {{ name }}</caption><thead><tr><th>Assets</th><th class="num-col">Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody>{{ pfs_html }}</tbody></table>
<p><strong>Credit:</strong> {{ credit_text }}</p></section>
<div class="pg-footer"><span>South River Capital &mdash; Credit Memorandum</span><span>Page 5 of 7</span></div>
</div>
<div class="page">
<section class="section"><h2 class="sec"><span class="num">X</span>Repayment &amp; Amortization</h2>
